= {!<span class="term term-religious">!}Ayatollah Abol-Qasem Kashani{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-religious">!}Kashani{!</span>!} is an independent political counterpart with his own constituency and
objectives—not a subordinate member of the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front's{!</span>!} staff. Cooperation can
mobilize religious and bazaar networks without dissolving that independence.

- @kashani_bazaar
- @kashani_terms
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@kashani_bazaar
title: Coordinate a bazaar appeal
subtitle: <span class="term term-religious">Kashani</span> carries the oil appeal through the bazaar and <span class="term term-religious">religious networks</span> on his own authority
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; religious_network_organization += 5; public_mandate += 3

{!<span class="term term-religious">!}Kashani{!</span>!}'s intermediaries and
the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} agree on
language that can travel
through bazaar and {!<span class="term term-religious">!}religious networks{!</span>!} while leaving their separate authority
visible. The appeal reaches people the secretariat could not summon directly.

The public campaign expands, but the new contacts belong to an allied network,
not to a staff apparatus under
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} command.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@kashani_terms
title: Negotiate terms of cooperation
subtitle: The agreement identifies where cooperation ends, preserving <span class="term term-religious">Kashani</span>'s independence as well as the <span class="term term-national-front">Front</span>'s
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; religious_network_relation += 5; religious_network_dissent -= 3

The meeting states what the two sides will coordinate, what they will decide
independently, and which public language neither will accept. The narrower
agreement prevents cooperation from being mistaken for subordination.

Relations improve under explicit terms. The political partnership remains
contingent rather than settled.

